thvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mfenced></math> is differentiable for all <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">R</mi><mo>.</mo></math> Then possible value (s) of a is (are)</td>\t\t\t<td><math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></td>\t\t\t<td>2</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td><math><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>)</mo></math></td>\t\t\t<td>Let <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#969;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>1</mn></math> be a complex cube roots of unity. If <math><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#969;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#969;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#969;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#969;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#969;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#969;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> then possible value (s) of n is (are)</td>\t\t\t<td><math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></td>\t\t\t<td>3</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td><math><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>)</mo></math></td>\t\t\t<td>Let the harmonic mean of two positive real numbers a and b 4. If q is a positive real number such that a, 5, q, b is an arithmetic progression, then the value (s) of |q &ndash; a| is (are)</td>\t\t\t<td><math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></td>\t\t\t<td>4</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">(T)</mi></math></td>\t\t\t<td>5</td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table>",
